(7474590, 1187302, 100831, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Teafran:</b></div><hr/><i> I should really recuse myself from reflection shots. Its a good idea, but lacks in execution.  For a reflection shot to work, you have to have more than just a reflection - it has to be balanced with something firmer - just an image of a reflection without context is meaningless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I disagree. Reflections, as in this case, can make excellent abstracts. They''re almost like snowflakes... no two are the same:)</td>', 'Originally posted by Teafran: I should really recuse myself from reflection shots. Its a good idea, but lacks in execution.  For a reflection shot to work, you have to have more than just a reflection - it has to be balanced with something firmer - just an image of a reflection without context is meaningless.   I disagree. Reflections, as in this case, can make excellent abstracts. They''re almost like snowflakes... no two are the same:)', '2016-09-19 09:36:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(7474594, 1187132, 114285, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the fun facts, very interesting. I liked this one, not so much the paving though, just wonder if you thought cropping it out.... I did a quick crop on my iPad, you know just zooming in and it looked good, just saying ;)</td>', 'Thanks for the fun facts, very interesting. I liked this one, not so much the paving though, just wonder if you thought cropping it out.... I did a quick crop on my iPad, you know just zooming in and it looked good, just saying ;)', '2016-09-19 10:18:40.000000', NULL, 0),
